# KEYS.asc: signing keys for sebastienrousseau/sebastienrousseau.github.io
#
# SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0 OR MIT
# Copyright (c) 2007-2026 Sebastien Rousseau
#
# This project signs commits and tags with an SSH ed25519 key, not GPG.
# The file is named KEYS.asc because that is the name tooling and auditors
# look for; its contents are in git's allowed_signers format (ssh-keygen -Y),
# which is what gpg.ssh.allowedSignersFile consumes.
#
# A separate GPG key exists for encrypted vulnerability reports only and
# never signs releases. See SECURITY.md. Do not confuse the two.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# Verify a release tag against this file
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
#
#   git clone https://github.com/sebastienrousseau/sebastienrousseau.github.io
#   cd sebastienrousseau.github.io
#   git config gpg.ssh.allowedSignersFile KEYS.asc
#   git tag -v v1.2.1
#
# Expected output ends with:
#
#   Good "git" signature for sebastienrousseau@users.noreply.github.com
#     with ED25519 key SHA256:f6FG+guRNtT3R36oQFS4oWCx1d10nm+BoaIL3Tkh1r4
#
# Verify a commit the same way:
#
#   git config gpg.ssh.allowedSignersFile KEYS.asc
#   git log --show-signature -1
#
# The git config above is repo-local. To verify without touching your
# configuration at all:
#
#   git -c gpg.ssh.allowedSignersFile=KEYS.asc tag -v v1.2.1
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# Cross-check the fingerprint out of band
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# A key file in the repository proves nothing on its own: an attacker
# who can rewrite the repo can rewrite this file. Cross-check the
# fingerprint against at least one independent source:
#
#   * GitHub's signing-key API (served by GitHub, not by this repo):
#       curl -s https://api.github.com/users/sebastienrousseau/ssh_signing_keys
#   * The "Verified" badge GitHub displays on tags and commits.
#
# Fingerprint (SHA256, ed25519):
#   SHA256:f6FG+guRNtT3R36oQFS4oWCx1d10nm+BoaIL3Tkh1r4
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# Allowed signers (ssh-keygen -Y / git allowed_signers format)
# principal(s) [namespaces=...] keytype base64-key
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
sebastienrousseau@users.noreply.github.com namespaces="git" ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIDjGRQyeM79nAb4GHcpGzXMKq7HE3xyEOev4gVsnBN1e sebastienrousseau@users.noreply.github.com
